  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arizona received $25.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $17.7B in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $6.2B. Total award count stands at 15,704 and the average award size is $1.6M. Obligations rose 8.1% year over year. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for $6.4B of obligations, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $6.1B. RAYTHEON COMPANY is the top vendor with $8.1B in obligations, followed by TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $4.7B and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO with $4.5B. Historical context shows obligations by fiscal year moved from $16.5B in FY21 to $25.2B in FY26. The FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial. This snapshot highlights where federal dollars are concentrated by agency, vendor, and industry, and the scale of obligations contracting officers have managed in Arizona during the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are driving federal contract spending in Arizona?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $17.7B in Arizona in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $6.2B. Other notable buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs with $369M and the General Services Administration with $209M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries capture the largest shares of Arizona contracting?",
        "body": "RAYTHEON COMPANY captured $8.1B in obligations and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP captured $4.7B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing led industries with $6.4B, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction followed with $6.1B."
      }
    ]
